        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/ea5d25/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-03T18:35:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Whan playing power cards. Do&nbsp;you have to target them when you play em or can you freestyle ?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Example. I have an idea if what a slow power will do, and i target it to a certain land. Then stuff happens during fast p - and invader phase. Now when slow Powers take effect, they dont have any value in the land i intendet to target it,&nbsp; cause the scenario has changed.&nbsp;Can i then change the target of my slow power to take effect in another land, as long as i follow the range / and Target rules.&nbsp; Or does the power just loose it´s effect in this turn ? Reading the rulebook i am thinking the answer to this question is NO. But i´m wondering, it kind of makes a big differance if Slow powers can be \"redirected\" dursing slow Power phase. It is a much easier game.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Thanks</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:50.719Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
